<title>HONG KONG: Tung Fong Hung year net rises sharply.</title>
<headline>Tung Fong Hung year net rises sharply.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended July 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   11.9	 vs 3.4 (adjusted)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    1.6	  vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  87.31 gain vs 20.06 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    101.16     vs 22.59</p>
<p>    Turnover		     714.83     vs 252.71</p>
<p>    Company name		 Tung Fong Hung (Holdings) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  December 18-27, 1996</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   January 20, 1997</p>
<p>NOTE - Tung Fong Hung is a retailer of Chinese medicines, health foods and dried seafood.</p>
<p>The company proposed a special dividend of 0.9 H.K. cents per share vs nil and bonus issue of new shares on the basis of one bonus share for every five existing shares.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain mainly on disposal of investment and other properties.</p>
<p>Comparative share earnings have been adjusted for a 1-for-5 bonus issue.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 5.5 H.K. cent (including interim dividend of three cents and special dividend) vs one cent.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
